From ub330c2028fed415b at groups.google.com  Fri Apr 29 01:47:01 2016
From: ub330c2028fed415b at groups.google.com (Phil Chalmers)
Date: Fri, 29 Apr 2016 01:47:01 +0000
Subject: Re: IIF bimodality and item misfit
Message-ID: <Rw8lcNlx3bQ.cU7wpvFdBAAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <Rw8lcNlx3bQ.7X8Rggn0AwAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
References: <Rw8lcNlx3bQ.7X8Rggn0AwAJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/Rw8lcNlx3bQ/m/cU7wpvFdBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

These items are basically step-function items similar to what you would find in latent class models. They generally aren't all that great for latent trait models because all they really tell you is who is above some exact latent trait level. So removing them might make the most sense, otherwise placing prior distributions on them may also help to pull the slopes away from ∞ (they also seem to have some sparse categories according to the intercept terms, which might be part of the problem). Cheers.

Phil

